{
  "name": "shitting_furiously",
  "description": "A hybrid ray tracing implementation that utilizes a unified Rust codebase for both host-side orchestration and GPU-resident compute kernels via the rust-gpu/SPIR-V toolchain. It leverages Vulkan compute pipelines for massively parallel ray-sphere intersection tests, while providing a Rayon-based multi-threaded CPU fallback for comparative performance analysis. The system integrates real-time display capabilities through the Piston framework and handles complex Vulkan state management including descriptor sets, command buffers, and memory-mapped storage buffers.",
